WEBVTT

cue-1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.457
Under your course's Manage Settings, 

cue-2
00:00:02.457 --> 00:00:06.200
scroll down to Curriculum and
click into the Scheduling & Assessment

cue-3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:12.720
Settings. Now we see a page with four tabs
of settings. In general, the Schedule tab

cue-4
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:17.120
lets you create a suggested course
timeline for students to follow. The

cue-5
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.340
Assessment Settings tab allows you to
configure each assessment item in more

cue-6
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:26.640
detail. The Student Expectations tab
enables you to set accommodations for

cue-7
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.340
individual students based on their needs.
Finally, Advanced Gating is for

cue-8
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:35.780
instructors who want more control over how
and when course materials become

cue-9
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:40.940
accessible. If you need help with Advanced
Gating, contact OLI Help at

cue-10
00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:47.920
oli-help@cmu.edu. Let's start with the
Scheduling setting. Here you will see

cue-11
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.260
your course timeline laid out across
weeks. Each line here represents a unit of

cue-12
00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.949
the course. Later, you will have an
adjustable schedule on this page. To start

cue-13
00:00:57.949 --> 00:01:03.460
with, click Set Schedule. Select the day
you want to consider for that schedule,

cue-14
00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:04.319
click Continue.

cue-15
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:10.100
If you choose Do Not Set Assessment Due
Dates, the system will not automatically

cue-16
00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:15.080
assign any due dates. You will need to
manually set them later in the Assessment

cue-17
00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:19.840
Setting view. If you choose Set Assessment
Due Dates According to the Sequence of

cue-18
00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:24.780
Course Content, due dates will align with
where each assessment appears within a

cue-19
00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:30.220
unit. For example, if an assessment is
placed halfway through a unit, its due

cue-20
00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:33.680
date will also be scheduled halfway
through that unit's duration.

cue-21
00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:39.220
If you choose Set Assessment Due Dates to
the End of Each Section, all assessments

cue-22
00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:44.180
will be due at the end of their respective
units. So even if an assessment appears

cue-23
00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:49.470
midway through that unit, its due date
will still be at the end of that unit.

cue-24
00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:55.720
This option is the most commonly used. Now
you will see a Gantt-style timeline. Use

cue-25
00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:00.900
Control plus minus or Command plus minus
to adjust the size of the content on the

cue-26
00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:05.900
screen for the best view. You can view or
hide details of a unit by clicking the

cue-27
00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:12.859
small black button or the Expand
All/Collapse All button. Length of each

cue-28
00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:17.920
block represent the suggested time
duration of the unit, which is independent

cue-29
00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:22.960
of assessment dates you set. They are
interactive and fully adjustable, meaning

cue-30
00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:28.260
that you can move it or drag the ends to
change when a unit begins or ends. You can

cue-31
00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:34.220
also search for a specific module or
topic using the search bar. By default,

cue-32
00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:40.120
items under Unit are set to Suggested By
Dates. Suggested By Date is for keeping

cue-33
00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:45.480
students on track, for example, with their
readings. While Due By Date is for

cue-34
00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:50.720
scored/graded objects. You can change one
item's date into Hard Due Dates or

cue-35
00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:55.900
In-Class Activity by clicking and editing
them on the bottom left-hand corner of the

cue-36
00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:56.400
screen.

cue-37
00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:03.520
The item will then change to a calendar or
group icon. You can also right-click a

cue-38
00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:09.970
unit or item to remove it, adjust dates
with numeric input given selected units or

cue-39
00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:15.150
assessment item, or drag and reposition
the task on the timeline.

cue-40
00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:21.020
This gives you granular control over how
students pace themselves. Remember to

cue-41
00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:26.140
click Save Changes after you are done. If
you want to preview the schedule from a

cue-42
00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:31.840
student view, go back to the course Manage
Settings. Click Preview as Student to see

cue-43
00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:38.040
what your learners will see. Recent items
will appear under Upcoming Agenda on the

cue-44
00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:42.560
homepage, and the full schedule can be
viewed on the Schedule page.

cue-45
00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:48.940
And that's the Scheduling tool. Remember,
you can change these settings at any time,

cue-46
00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:53.660
even after the course has begun. In the
next video, we'll walk through the

cue-47
00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:54.920
Assessment Settings.
